 "notes": "A long barn on its own axis north-south: thick walls of local stone about 3.4 m high under a dark corrugated-metal pitched roof, its gable ends clad dark with the V-shaped glazed truss and a pale rendered panel below (the end elevation and the dusk views). From the aerial: the pitched hall down the middle, a flat-roofed strip of service rooms along the east side with the entrance gap in its middle (the white doors either side of the open gate in the long-side views), and a cane pergola on steel posts over stone footings along the west side, where the hall opens toward the Andes. Around it a gravel yard, rows of vines, bare poplar windbreaks, and the long reflecting basin seen in the sunset view. Guessed: exact length (~40 m) and roof pitch from door heights, the basin's position east of the building, the placing of west openings, and the semi-underground barrel cellar to the south, which is not visible outside and is not modelled."
